CORRECTION to this commit MESSAGE (the commit CONTENT is correct and unaffected).

The sentence beginning "The new render code earns its place here:" lost its two-word
subject. It should read:

    ... earns its place here: the wakerctl-watches line now reports NO EVIDENCE naming
    the unreadable state dir instead of the bare "none" it printed two hours ago while
    one watch was armed on the cluster ...

CAUSE: the message was passed through a zsh -c string in which that subject was wrapped
in backticks, so zsh ran it as command substitution. It failed ("command not found:
wakerctl") and substituted the empty string. Same author, same session, fourth instance of
this shell-quoting class -- the other three were piping a command whose exit status I then
read, which reported the pipe tail status instead.

WHY A NOTE AND NOT AN AMEND: the commit is already pushed to a branch other sessions share,
so rewriting it would need a force-push; and any NEW commit on main would move HEAD, making
the LIVE-STATE.md this very commit carries stale again (freshness is Git: == HEAD or HEAD^).
A note annotates without either cost. Fetch with:
    git fetch origin "refs/notes/*:refs/notes/*"
